Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:08:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 10 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 2, row A5): A QUOTATION UNDER A PATH THAT DOES
 NOT EXIST IS NOT FOUND IN THE FILE NAMED; AND B1892'S LOCK HOLDS ITS VERDICT
 AND THE COLUMNS OF ITS ANSWERS

A reader's check of main's answers at Review 80 (agy-002's; row A5, not checked by main). Three false passes
remain in B1892's quotation checker and lock. Two are made again here and mended. The third is in the
reader's file, which is read through a mask: it is not built.

ONE, in the checker. Where the path a finding names was not at the commit, every file whose name ends as the
path does was taken in its place. A quotation of B1881's page, set under a path that does not exist and ends
in FINDINGS.md, was placed "named" and reported as found. A path that is at no commit read is no file now:
the placing says "no such file", and the kept result counts those. No finding of the four readers' files
names such a path, so no kept count moves: each result file gains one field, with 0.

THE SAME FAULT STOOD IN B1894'S CHECKER, by a patch of this series (part 3's seventeenth), which gave it
B1892's placing before main wrote that the placing was not to be copied. It is mended the same way. One test
of B1894's lock, written by that patch, named a path that is not at the commit read; it is changed under a
dated note.

TWO, in the lock of B1892. It read the verdict file for its id, the names of its scope and its last words,
and the answers for the names of their rows. A changed verdict, a replaced verdict line and emptied columns
of the answers passed. The lock now holds the verdict, the verdict line by three of its sentences, that each
of the 99 rows of the answers has its four cells and each says something, and that the rows marked as sent
to the builder are the ones the count names. Six planted changes pass what the lock asked before and are
reported now.

What this does not hold, said here: a cell of the answers reworded to other words of some length.

Run: the planted case on both checkers, on the commit before (placed "named"; found) and on the patch ("no
such file"; not found). Both checkers run again in a clone that holds the four readers' commits: the counts
main kept, and the new field. The locks of B1892 and B1894: 13 tests pass. Every gate passes but the count
of landings.

Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote the mends.
